{"type":"FeatureCollection","metadata":{"description":"Approximate West Orange elementary attendance zones, drawn on 2020 Census blocks and assigned from the West Orange Board of Education Street Directory (revised June 5, 2026). Each street the directory lists for a single elementary school was matched by name to OpenStreetMap street geometry, and every point in the district was first given the school of its nearest such street (a 24 m grid). Each census block then took the school covering most of it. Blocks split between schools (the second school covering at least 15% of the block and about 1 hectare, or at least 35% of the block and about half a hectare) were divided along a smoothed version of that grid, so edges inside those blocks are interpolated, not surveyed. Streets split between schools by house number were not used to draw zones, so edges near them are approximate. Use the district's street directory, not this file, to confirm an address.","sources":["West Orange Board of Education, Street Directory, revised 2026-06-05, https://www.woboe.org/departments/transportation/street-directory","OpenStreetMap contributors (ODbL), street geometry retrieved via Overpass API 2026-10-22","U.S. Census Bureau, TIGERweb 2020 Census Blocks and County Subdivisions (West Orange township, GEOID 3401379800), retrieved 2026-10-22; the district outline is the township boundary"],"built":"2026-10-22","rules":["Four unpopulated blocks bordered mostly by another school take the school they share the longest border with.","Inside split blocks, pieces under about 1 hectare (or under a fifth of the block, for blocks smaller than 5 hectares) were given to the school covering most of the block.","Detached pieces were kept only where the directory assigns a street, or a house-number range on a street, in that piece to that school. Three pieces were merged into the neighboring zone: 0.03% of Redwood and 1.1% of Washington, which held no such street, and 0.22% of St. Cloud, which held only part of a street split by house number.","Boundaries simplified with a shared-edge (coverage) simplification at about 8 m, so neighboring zones share the same edges, with no gaps or overlaps beyond rounding (under 15 square meters)."],"method_check":"Consistency check, not an accuracy test: of 1,409 OpenStreetMap points on 77 streets the directory assigns to a single elementary school, 98.9% fall inside that school's zone in this file (99.0% for the earlier grid-only version). The check uses the same directory the zones were built from, so it shows the census-block step kept the directory assignments; it cannot show the directory itself is complete. Computed in a browser session on 2026-10-22; not reproducible from this repository alone.","license_note":"Street geometry from OpenStreetMap, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors, available under the Open Database License (ODbL). Census geography is public domain."},"district":{"type":"Feature","properties":{"name":"West Orange Public Schools"},"geometry":{"type":"Polygon","coordinates":[[[-74.30218,40.76347],[-74.30006,40.76807],[-74.29899,40.77037],[-74.29837,40.77164],[-74.29809,40.7723],[-74.29667,40.77509],[-74.29439,40.77964],[-74.28709,40.7943],[-74.28528,40.79763],[-74.28271,40.8025],[-74.28227,40.80351],[-74.28116,40.80562],[-74.27957,40.80865],[-74.27623,40.81494],[-74.27527,40.81666],[-74.27371,40.81918],[-74.26897,40.82679],[-74.26476,40.82507],[-74.26372,40.82502],[-74.26354,40.82503],[-74.25207,40.82449],[-74.251,40.82442],[-74.23229,40.81433],[-74.23237,40.81347],[-74.23281,40.81286],[-74.23433,40.81226],[-74.23484,40.81056],[-74.23538,40.80964],[-74.23564,40.80838],[-74.23604,40.80763],[-74.23672,40.80671],[-74.2373,40.80559],[-74.23773,40.80353],[-74.23657,40.80254],[-74.23539,40.80161],[-74.2345,40.80083],[-74.22817,40.79572],[-74.22744,40.79512],[-74.22677,40.79458],[-74.22601,40.79399],[-74.22377,40.79224],[-74.22057,40.78978],[-74.22116,40.78928],[-74.22481,40.78623],[-74.22493,40.78629],[-74.22673,40